00:30:40.485 --> 00:30:43.685
for the community center, just to kind of let you all know.

00:30:44.470 --> 00:30:49.830
So one thing we had to do is we had to switch to an interior attic access.

00:30:50.230 --> 00:30:53.190
We had originally proposed to the contractor

00:30:54.230 --> 00:30:56.550
accessing through gable end vents.

00:30:58.015 --> 00:31:07.375
And so the contractor asked me to talk to the building official prior to them putting that in, because the contractor was pretty convinced under the current

00:31:07.855 --> 00:31:09.135
zoning regs

00:31:09.720 --> 00:31:13.800
that was not code compliant. So I checked with the building official.

00:31:14.840 --> 00:31:19.800
It did in fact turn out not to be code compliant in the latest code cycle.

00:31:20.280 --> 00:31:22.840
You're no longer allowed to have gable and vents

00:31:23.305 --> 00:31:24.745
in addition to

00:31:25.385 --> 00:31:26.025
and

00:31:26.185 --> 00:31:27.305
bridge venting.

00:31:27.385 --> 00:31:31.945
So we took that out and switched to interior access to the attic.

00:31:32.585 --> 00:31:34.265
We had the contractor

00:31:34.505 --> 00:31:37.145
build a walkway

00:31:36.730 --> 00:31:39.290
that's about 20 inches off the,

00:31:39.690 --> 00:31:44.730
what will be the ceiling of the 1st Floor. So when it's fully insulated,

00:31:45.130 --> 00:31:52.695
there will still be a pathway that you can walk essentially from one end of the building to the other without disturbing the insulation.

00:31:53.095 --> 00:31:56.855
And that ties into the interior attic access location.

00:31:57.895 --> 00:32:00.535
There will not be storage in the attic,

00:32:01.130 --> 00:32:04.170
but there will be access for future maintenance.

00:32:05.210 --> 00:32:07.290
As far as exterior lighting,

00:32:07.850 --> 00:32:09.690
what we did was we

00:32:10.570 --> 00:32:13.770
asked that the electrician

00:32:13.425 --> 00:32:16.225
put in a central timer

00:32:16.865 --> 00:32:18.945
that runs essentially off an

00:32:20.145 --> 00:32:24.865
atomic clock so we can have the exterior lighting only run

00:32:25.025 --> 00:32:25.345
when

00:32:26.580 --> 00:32:28.660
you know, during evening hours.

00:32:29.140 --> 00:32:35.780
So they have they're going to do a central one as opposed to individual ones for each of the lights, which makes a lot of sense.

00:32:36.340 --> 00:32:38.660
We didn't want just a light sensor

00:32:38.740 --> 00:32:40.740
because given some of the other lighting

00:32:41.835 --> 00:32:43.035
that's out there

00:32:43.355 --> 00:32:46.635
and the floodlights, I didn't want it to stay tripped off.

00:32:47.195 --> 00:32:48.635
So we did

00:32:49.195 --> 00:32:53.275
we reworked a little bit what we're doing for the bathrooms.

00:32:54.250 --> 00:32:56.730
There will be a common switched

00:32:56.730 --> 00:32:59.130
fan light combination in the bathroom,

00:33:00.010 --> 00:33:04.570
but the bathroom with the shower will also have an additional humidistat.

00:33:04.890 --> 00:33:07.290
So it runs long enough to remove the humidity,

00:33:09.075 --> 00:33:10.355
is pretty important

00:33:10.515 --> 00:33:14.275
when you're using ductless splits as your heating and cooling source.

00:33:15.635 --> 00:33:19.875
We also switch most of the lighting in the building

00:33:20.355 --> 00:33:21.555
just from

00:33:21.875 --> 00:33:23.315
standalone pucks

00:33:24.540 --> 00:33:27.740
to conventional can lights

00:33:28.140 --> 00:33:28.860
with

00:33:28.940 --> 00:33:30.300
essentially

00:33:30.300 --> 00:33:31.580
an LED,

00:33:32.380 --> 00:33:33.100
you know,

00:33:33.500 --> 00:33:35.980
LED light source that goes in it.

00:33:36.380 --> 00:33:37.100
Those will be

00:33:38.525 --> 00:33:39.965
variable Kelvin,

00:33:40.125 --> 00:33:42.365
so you can change the light temperature

00:33:42.605 --> 00:33:46.845
of the room. And we'll have to, once we start picking colors,

00:33:47.325 --> 00:33:50.925
wall covers, colors, we'll have to start figuring about what,

00:33:51.410 --> 00:33:55.490
you know, how blue or how red we want the lights

00:33:55.730 --> 00:33:57.410
in each of the rooms.

00:33:57.570 --> 00:34:00.370
We also worked hard to make sure that the

00:34:01.170 --> 00:34:04.130
lights in that main large room

